+## Native v4 measurements and residual diagnostic candidate
+
+The v4 Plan `85d2d63856d825c8da29b162dfc6798230a90f0584e75941b98e96ace42778d8`
+ran source `6f650cb9c981317b970dad0abae6846165f80166` on 2026-10-12. Compilation,
+reader CTest (1/1), native tests (13/13) and both original-byte Beacon binders passed.
+The candidate executable SHA256 is
+`54f0ce337fda98acfeb75e54e538d4936f820d42f530589060f6ac65966d3398` and its combined
+tool/zlib source digest is `667c9aef556aafd55021eeec5b968bcc9786d1fa3ebbcf6f18e67af6be22c3f0`.
+The variant measured bytecode 1480/1480 and stack 1808/1808; the original measured
+1455/1455 and 1394/1394. External dependency absence and runtime gates stayed false.
+
+The original root exited zero but one unidentified job member remained beyond
+the two-second drain. The original job was stopped, zero members confirmed and
+the lease released; overall `Success=false` remains authoritative. Preserve
+`build/native-header-fixed-20261012` and the candidate executable. Supervision SHA256
+is `4b95208c4ad5ae2ea758ff2c8463429d4950665463735e4223d1246c77c134b0`; candidate
+build receipt SHA256 is `7ff2f0fe81dbc6891b931196ae7efd664727ec8d83f67935135a244ce6633731`.
+The member was not identified at the time and must not be called harmless telemetry.
+
+The next source candidate reuses the unchanged `Rig.JobMembers.cs`, SHA256
+`5a02254764277b62f752792f1ec4f5b93b85237b171a3381a78d58f6af190e91`, from the reviewed
+Material/Rig observer family. Its original job handle is borrowed read-only,
+enumeration is bounded to 64 members, and each process is queried through a limited
+query handle for image, creation, parent PID and `IsProcessInJob`. No new owner,
+PID kill, environment switch or shared-provider modification is introduced.
+
+Our CMake/MSBuild chain does not satisfy the existing compiler classifier's direct
+child, single compiler generation and compiler-PID receipt requirements. Therefore
+this instrumentation is **diagnostic only**. The first residual observation records
+members before any owned stop. `diagnostics.ps1` hashes only complete observed
+member image files under read guards, capped at 64 MiB per image and 128 MiB total,
+with a 1,000 ms observation budget checked during streaming and after native calls.
+Blocking native/filesystem calls cannot be preempted; late observations are recorded
+incomplete and their cost still consumes the unchanged two-second drain. The hash
+attests image file bytes, not loaded memory or a safe telemetry classification.
+Observation and hash failures remain visible and never grant build acceptance.
+Native helper loading occurs only after full resource admission; Plan loads none.
+
+The 37 existing supervision and 38 registration/quarantine mock checks still pass.
+Twenty-five additional diagnostic checks cover source-file hashing, identity and
+capture failures, size/count/time policy, single observation, fresh closure and
+callback time charged to the drain. They use mocks plus one small managed source
+file hash; no observer native type, compiler, process, lease or game is launched.
+
